<h1>Manage GitHub Connection</h1>

<p>Currently connected to <strong><%= @installation.repo_full_name %></strong>.</p>

<h2>Change the selected repository</h2>
<p>
  Updating an existing github installation in place is not supported (GitHub won't tell
  Delve that the selected repository/permissions have changed). To work from a different
  repository, or change the granted permissions, you need to uninstall and reinstall the
  GitHub app.
</p>
<ol>
  <li>
    Uninstall the app from
    <%= link_to "your GitHub app settings", "https://github.com/settings/installations", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>.
  </li>
  <li>Disconnect below, so Delve stops holding onto a token GitHub has already revoked.</li>
  <li><%= link_to "Reinstall it", @install_url %>, picking the repository you want this time.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Uninstall the app entirely</h2>
<p>
  If you'd rather remove Delve's access to GitHub completely, just do step 1 above
  (<%= link_to "your GitHub app settings", "https://github.com/settings/installations", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>)
  and then disconnect below.
</p>

<h2>Danger zone</h2>
<p>Disconnecting removes Delve's stored GitHub token. You'll need to reconnect before you can resume editing content.</p>
<%= button_to "Disconnect GitHub", github_disconnect_path, method: :delete, class: "contrast", data: {confirm: "Disconnect GitHub? You will need to reconnect to keep editing content."} %>

<p><%= link_to "Back to Build", build_root_path %></p>
